			"id": "agent-analysis-rdb-preference-telemetry-pipeline",
			"interpretation": "Scope: HMOS World telemetry persistence: an RDB store feeding a click/exposure upload pipeline. TrackManager resets preference APP_TRACK_DATA, builds TrackCommonData from BUNDLE_INFO and deviceInfo, awaits TrackTable.getRdbStore (failures only logged), then starts a 60s interval with 'willClick' and 'navDestinationSwitch' UIObserver listeners. willClick resolves TRACK_KEY-marked nodes by recursive child-or-ancestor search; page switches stamp the prior page EXPOSURE with duration since pageSwitchInTime; reportData defaults pageName to currentPage and maps '' pageName/interactionContent to null. Each tick: queryAll -> rows mapped to TrackModel -> TrackService.postTrackData; resolved -> deleteTrackData; rejected -> delete only when row count > 1000. TrackTable maps TrackServiceData to rows of the 13-column trackTable (eventType/time non-null, rest null) and back via sealData, omitting null fields except eventType/time; deleteTrackData awaits full-table delete then the sqlite_sequence reset. RdbStore opens 'hmosWorldDatabase.db' (S1); insert/deleteAll run as @Concurrent taskpool tasks reopening the store per call, errors swallowed; query returns [] on failure; resetId uses the cached store. TrackModel/TrackServiceData/TrackEventType/TRACK_KEY come from ../model/TrackModel.ets. Contract: keep store name, null-vs-absent roundtrip, delete-only-on-success vs >1000-flush, sequence reset stable. postTrackData is an Oracle dependency: Promise<boolean> that here only resolves true.",
			"kind": "analysis",
			"limitations": ["TrackService.postTrackData contains no upload path: Promise.resolve(true) makes the reject branch unreachable in this tree, so the meaning of a false or rejected result is unevidenced here.","RdbStore.deleteAll and RdbStore.query log-and-recover internally, so insert/delete failures and empty queries look alike to TrackManager; actual device behavior of these taskpool paths is not exercised here."],
